WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:03.530
Unit two. Styling with CSS!

2
00:00:04.502 --> 00:00:09.074
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:12.198
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.248 --> 00:00:15.981
Today we learn about Styling with CSS. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.644 --> 00:00:21.602
CSS. Say it with me. CSS!

6
00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:28.936
Style. Say it with me. Style!

7
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:35.817
Color. Say it with me. Color!

8
00:00:39.327 --> 00:00:43.216
Selector. Say it with me. Selector!

9
00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:50.087
Property. Say it with me. Property!

10
00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:57.269
Value. Say it with me. Value!

11
00:01:00.771 --> 00:01:04.571
Layout. Say it with me. Layout!

12
00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:11.968
Design. Say it with me. Design!

13
00:01:15.421 --> 00:01:29.149
CSS controls the style of a web page, like color and layout. A selector chooses which element to style, and a property sets a value like font size. Good CSS design makes a page both attractive and easy to read.

14
00:01:29.199 --> 00:01:32.785
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:33.978 --> 00:01:39.375
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:40.561
Color!

17
00:01:41.292 --> 00:01:46.720
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.920
Layout!

19
00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:56.758
Did you know? CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets, and the word 'cascading' means styles can build on top of each other!

20
00:01:56.808 --> 00:01:59.135
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:09.652
Think and answer. How does CSS change the way a webpage looks without changing its content?

22
00:02:09.702 --> 00:02:10.852
Great answer!

23
00:02:12.013 --> 00:02:17.797
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.847 --> 00:02:21.232
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

